      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for ibuprofen.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.\n- **Daily total:** The maximum is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use in adults. Most patients should get less, and the OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Risks at this dose:** It carries a high risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** (a typical dose for analgesia or inflammation)\n- **1600 mg total per day, divided** (for example, 400 mg four times daily)\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. Otherwise, tell me which dose to enter."
      }
